{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/authenticateDevice()"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"code":"authenticateDevice()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mTLS device login (CONTRACT.md §6.1 rules 6-10)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@discardableResult"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"authenticateDevice"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","text":"AxiamClient"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC17DeviceLoginResultV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/DeviceLoginResult","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Issues "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/device"},{"type":"text","text":" with no request body."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reachable only on a client configured with a client certificate"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 7,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/clientCertificate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). On any other client this refuses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CLIENT-SIDE with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"zero wire calls","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"certificate the server would answer ","type":"text"},{"code":"401","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" regardless, so going to the wire would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only turn a configuration mistake into an authentication failure.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On success the returned token is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adopted as this client’s credential","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a "},{"code":"login()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" result is (rule 6): every subsequent REST call this client sends —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including every "},{"code":"management()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" operation — carries it as "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer <token>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and withholds this client’s own cookie jar, so a session cookie from an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier "},{"code":"login()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can never ride alongside it. The server reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"axiam_access","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie before "},{"code":"Authorization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so keeping a stale one would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently run every later request as the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"previous","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" session’s principal, defeating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the point of authenticating fresh."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no refresh token"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" for this credential (rule 6, D-6 of the dogfooding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan): the §9 single-flight guard has nothing to spend on it, so a later "},{"code":"401","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on this call, or on any request this client sends afterward — is surfaced as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no refresh attempt","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". The caller recovers by calling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"authenticateDevice()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" again, which costs one TLS handshake."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every refusal is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 8, server T22.4): an unknown, untrusted,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expired, revoked or unbound certificate, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Server","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-type certificate, all map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"429","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the route’s per-IP rate limiter maps to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (§2), never ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"mapError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already keeps the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart, so this method adds no special-casing for it, and it is never retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The token is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"certificate-bound"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"cnf.x5t#S256","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") when AXIAM itself terminated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the TLS handshake (rule 9); ","type":"text"},{"code":"DeviceLoginResult.tokenType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"Bearer\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"way. A resource server verifying it locally MUST use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator.authenticateSenderConstrained(_:presentedThumbprint:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or thread ","type":"text"},{"code":"PresentedProofs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" through ","type":"text"},{"code":"authenticate(_:presentedProofs:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than the plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"authenticate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which — after this SDK’s own §10.1 rule 9 fix","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— refuses a bound token with no evidence.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" client-side (no certificate configured, zero"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wire calls) or from the server’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/network(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or any other non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"200"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/authenticatedevice()"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC18authenticateDeviceAC0E11LoginResultVyYaKF","title":"authenticateDevice()","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"authenticateDevice"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC","text":"AxiamClient"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC17DeviceLoginResultV","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/DeviceLoginResult":{"title":"AxiamClient.DeviceLoginResult","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/deviceloginresult","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"authenticateDevice()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" result (CONTRACT.md §6.1 rule 6)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/DeviceLoginResult"},"doc://AxiamSDK/do